cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "EQ-Scalculator: Earthquake Scaling Relationship Calculator"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file, and also cite the underlying scaling-relation publications listed in the README."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: James
    family-names: La Greca
    affiliation: "University of Melbourne"
    # TODO: add your ORCID here, e.g.
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/james-lagreca/EQ-Scalculator"
url: "https://james-lagreca.github.io/EQ-Scalculator/"
abstract: >-
  A client-side web application for calculating, comparing and exploring
  empirical earthquake fault-scaling relationships. It solves published
  relations between moment magnitude, seismic moment, rupture length, width,
  area, surface rupture length, and average and maximum displacement, in both
  directions, with piecewise (multi-segment) support, unit conversion,
  Monte Carlo uncertainty propagation, multi-model comparison and chained
  calculations. Coefficients are transcribed from the primary literature and
  checked by an automated self-consistency verification suite.
keywords:
  - earthquake
  - fault scaling
  - seismic hazard
  - magnitude-area scaling
  - rupture dimensions
  - stable continental region
  - seismology
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
